  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Among Gu Masters gathering for the three kings inheritance on San Cha mountain, he is young clan leader of Yun clan who reached rank three peak stage at twenty-three and, at thirty-five, stands a step away from rank four peak stage.",
      "chapters": [
        375
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_masters",
        "evt_arc_three_kings_inheritance",
        "loc_san_cha_mountain",
        "fac_yun_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He wears white clothing with wide sleeves that sway with the wind, and he has a handsome face.",
      "chapters": [
        376
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "At an inheritance entrance he wears white clothing with wide sleeves and a handsome face when he blocks Fang Yuan and Bai Ning Bing. He accuses Fang Yuan of killing Tie Ba Xiu unfairly with a flying Gu. He says they already let Tie Ruo Nan go first because they admire Tie Mu Bai, then presses Fang Yuan to stand down after that unfair victory because so many heroes and geniuses are waiting and it is not Fang Yuan’s turn yet. Fang Yuan yields the queue, and Yun Luo Tian enters. Nearby talk treats Yun clan as first-class rather than a super clan. His conduct is inspected as representing Yun clan’s image, and he expects the exchange to raise Yun clan’s standing in the righteous faction. He had wanted a fight after years of closed cultivation on flying skills, but Fang Yuan’s courteous reply leaves him without an opening.",
      "chapters": [
        376
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "entrance-challenge",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_bai_ning_bing",
        "char_tie_ba_xiu",
        "char_tie_ruo_nan",
        "char_tie_mu_bai"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Inside the inheritance he meets Bai Ning Bing again as an opponent after the land spirit guides her through King Quan Inheritance rounds. He boasts that she does not have half his dogs, then panics when her dog army far outnumbers his.",
      "chapters": [
        381
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "defeat-and-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "inh_king_quan_inheritance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "He tries two exit tokens meant to protect him as young clan leader, but both fail, and he warns that killing him would offend Yun clan; Bai Ning Bing answers that she does not fear that house. A dog bites his throat and kills him. Bai Ning Bing keeps his Gu worms, then the land spirit sends his corpse to Fang Yuan.",
      "chapters": [
        382
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "defeat-and-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sources conflict:",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "defeat-and-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The question is open.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "defeat-and-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The enslavement path Gu worms he gained in King Quan Inheritance also benefit Bai Ning Bing. Fang Yuan uses beast strength placenta Gu to devour Yun Luo Tian’s aperture beside Wang Xiao.",
      "chapters": [
        382
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "defeat-and-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_beast_strength_placenta_gu",
        "char_wang_xiao"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A later rebirth recall restates that same devouring of both apertures.",
      "chapters": [
        399
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "defeat-and-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "After that rebirth, Fang Yuan again uses beast strength placenta Gu to devour Wang Xiao’s and Yun Luo Tian’s apertures.",
      "chapters": [
        400
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
